! GAPS deck: Line positive-sequence collapse at LINECODE FETCH (Pascal
! TLineObj.FetchLineCode -> RecalcElementData, Line.pas:572, reading the live
! ActiveCircuit.PositiveSequence, Line.pas:1085). With CktModel=Positive set
! BEFORE `linecode=`, the code's asymmetric sequence data (r1<>r0 etc.)
! collapses R0:=R1, X0:=X1, C0:=C1 at fetch time -- visible on readback
! (probed vs the pinned oracle 2026-07-25) and in the YPrim. Feature-sensitive:
! without `Set CktModel=Positive` the line keeps the code's R0 0.5 <> R1 0.1.
Clear
New Circuit.gaps_lps_lc basekv=12.47 phases=3
Set CktModel=Positive
New LineCode.lcps nphases=3 r1=0.1 x1=0.2 c1=3.0 r0=0.5 x0=0.9 c0=1.2 units=kft
New Line.llc bus1=sourcebus bus2=b1 length=1 linecode=lcps
New Load.ld bus1=b1 phases=3 kv=12.47 kw=1200 pf=0.95
Set voltagebases=[12.47]
Calcvoltagebases
Solve
